\begin{itemize}
  \item Encoder and decoder stacks of $N = 6$ layers; decoder self-attention is \textbf{masked} to stay autoregressive.
  \item Sinusoidal encodings $PE_{(pos, 2i)} = \sin\big(pos / 10000^{2i/d_{\text{model}}}\big)$ make relative positions easy to attend to.
  \item Learning-rate warm-up followed by inverse-square-root decay; label smoothing $\epsilon_{ls} = 0.1$.
\end{itemize}

\section{Complexity}
Self-attention costs $\mathcal{O}(n^2 d)$ per layer with $\mathcal{O}(1)$ sequential operations and maximum path length, versus $\mathcal{O}(n d^2)$ and $\mathcal{O}(n)$ for recurrence --- the source of both its parallelism and its quadratic-context problem (see Eq.~\eqref{eq:attn}).
